# sent_id = 1
# text = Now their dead were not numbered because of the greatness of their numbers; neither were the dead of the Nephites numbered-- but it came to pass after they had buried their dead, and also after the days of fasting, and mourning, and prayer, (and it was in the sixteenth year of the reign of the judges over the people of Nephi) there began to be continual peace throughout all the land.
# llm_note = Main clause: 'dead were not numbered' (passive); 'neither were ... numbered' = inversion per spec §5: neither=ADV advmod on 22-numbered, were=aux:pass, dead=nsubj:pass, 22-numbered=conj of 6-numbered; 'but ... there began to be peace' introduces new main clause with parataxis pivot; 'there' at token 70 is expletive of 71-began; parenthetical year-clause is parataxis on began; 'began to be continual peace' = began+xcomp(be)+nsubj(peace)
